# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for tests/test_stage (make -C tests tsan).
#
# vm_stage_apply writes the settings (switches, minimum size, statistics,
# GPU-safe, verify, overlapped-read mode, the learnt copy cost it resets) as
# single aligned words that the I/O hooks read without a lock, by design: a
# request uses whichever value it read, and each value is valid on its own.
# Everything that hands memory between threads (the helper's job, its
# buffers, their release) is synchronised and is not suppressed.
race:vm_stage_apply
